    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d759">

                <pb facs="0857" n="771" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg771"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-08-31"><hi rendition="#italic">August 31,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that he has just received the following telegram from
                    Admiral Cotton, dated Geneva, August 30:</p>
                <p>“<hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">San
                        Francisco</hi> sail to-day Beirut. Expect arrive there Friday. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Machias</hi> from Port Said yesterday.”</p>
                <p>Mr. Leishman inquires if the Department wishes him to communicate the above
                    information officially to the Sublime Porte.)</p>
            </div>
